  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e965f9168c2046c28c59aa4b83cc1ec, type: 3}
  m_Name: GravityBridge
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-gravitybridge
  DisplayIndex: 17
  DisplayName: Build your own bridge
  Shape: 16
  TeachingHint: Park the ball. Tilt to seat the hinged bridge, then cross the gap.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 5361834350392552374, guid: c5ca2bc4211254f5191d9bb1a59833fe, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: Keep the steel ball in the holding bay while gravity folds the
    bridge into its receiving jaw. Actual receiver contact engages an ideal mechanical
    retaining catch at the reached angle. Cross the physical bridge into the exit
    bay. Reset releases the catch and restores the folded bridge. Shared exit assist
    pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate
    gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must still physically clear the bore before
    completion.
